PATCH 635: restore the task-mode BYTE owner, SS task pointer and actual getter-to-setter AL.

Original startup DA47 CALL FAR SS:[354] reads MOV AL,CS:[2d59]; DA4b
CALL FAR SS:[358] consumes that returned AL. Getter2082:2d2a maps to
image123ba; actual engine callerCS1119 derives image basef690, so CS:2d59
maps to123e9. The emitted WORD at12d59 instead aliases code bytesff78.
Both MOV AL and XCHG AL operands are BYTE, as is22ec's TEST CS:[2d59].
Correct the shared mode definition, retaining neighboring bytes and reusing
that owner for existing reads. Setter reads SS:ea2c/ea2e through rebased
SS1c00, not old129's placeholder2ba9. LES/task store writes incomingAL to
ES:[DI+496] only when the far pointer is non-null, with WORD offset wrap;
XCHG returns the old mode byte regardless of the task pointer.
Use typed byte calls in the actual post-create d99b pair; no seeded mode
value or incomingEA substitutes for the measured getter result.

Sources: image123ba..123df andDA47..DA4f. Reproduce the original natural,
nonzero, independent-input and null-pointer cases with
python3 -B tools/oracle/capture_task_mode.py --output /tmp/wasm-fist-task-source.
The compact receipt in tools/oracle/task_mode_case.json binds original
CS mapping, full architectural states and16-MiB writes to the source image
and capture scripts. Actual getter entry through setter return spans
14/14/14/12 fetches; restored controls preserve all39 original frames,
27518 mixed samples and600-ms endpoint without clock adjustment.
Eight parent failures and both-target all-memory behavior cases cover this
BYTE contract. Original raw/lazy flags, preserved upperEAX and far CALL/RETF
guest-stack effects remain separate port CPU contracts. Handler depth/error
owners2d58/2d5a, generic DOS IRQ behavior,
production instruction/device time and complete frame/mixed PCM stay open.
